targets=
text=[@%0athere are a few options to enable swap in ltsp.%0a%0a(this assumes an ltsp dir of /opt/ltsp, and achitecture of i386, adjust to your%0aconfiguration if necessary)%0a%0a%0ausing local swap partitions from the hard disk:%0a%0aadd to /opt/ltsp/i386/etc/lts.conf:%0a%0a[Default]%0aUSE_LOCAL_SWAP=Y%0a%0a%0anetwork swap using NBD:%0a%0atouch /opt/ltsp/i386/etc/nbd-client%0a%0ain /opt/ltsp/i386/etc/lts.conf:%0a%0a[Default]%0aNBD_SWAP=Y%0a%0a%0aapt-get install nbd-server%0a%0aupdate-inetd --group LTSP --add "9210 stream tcp nowait nobody /usr/sbin/tcpd /usr/sbin/nbdswapd"%0a%0a%0aencrypting swap space:%0a%0ain /opt/ltsp/i386/etc/lts.conf:%0a%0aENCRYPT_SWAP=Y%0a%0aand install the cryptsetup package:%0a%0achroot /opt/ltsp/i386 apt-get install cryptsetup%0a%0a%0aalternately, you can configure nbd-server the hard way:%0a%0aapt-get install nbd-server%0a%0ain /etc/nbd-server:%0a%0aNBD_PORT[0]=9210%0aNBD_FILE[0]=/opt/ltsp/swap/swapfile.%25s%0aNBD_SERVER_OPTS[0]=""%0a%0ainvoke-rc.d nbd-server start%0a%0a%0acreate a file for each possible ip address that will attempt%0ato connect to the server:%0a%0a# size in megabytes%0asize=100%0ayour_ip_addresses="10.0.2.2 10.0.2.3 10.0.2.4 ..."%0amkdir -p /opt/ltsp/swap/%0afor a in $your_ip_addresse ; do%0a  dd if=/dev/zero of=/opt/ltsp/swap/swapfile.$a bs=1024k count=$size%0adone%0a@]
time=1239067635
author:1239067635=ok
diff:1239067635:1239067635:=1,65d0%0a%3c [@%0a%3c there are a few options to enable swap in ltsp.%0a%3c %0a%3c (this assumes an ltsp dir of /opt/ltsp, and achitecture of i386, adjust to your%0a%3c configuration if necessary)%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c using local swap partitions from the hard disk:%0a%3c %0a%3c add to /opt/ltsp/i386/etc/lts.conf:%0a%3c %0a%3c [Default]%0a%3c USE_LOCAL_SWAP=Y%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c network swap using NBD:%0a%3c %0a%3c touch /opt/ltsp/i386/etc/nbd-client%0a%3c %0a%3c in /opt/ltsp/i386/etc/lts.conf:%0a%3c %0a%3c [Default]%0a%3c NBD_SWAP=Y%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c apt-get install nbd-server%0a%3c %0a%3c update-inetd --group LTSP --add "9210 stream tcp nowait nobody /usr/sbin/tcpd /usr/sbin/nbdswapd"%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c encrypting swap space:%0a%3c %0a%3c in /opt/ltsp/i386/etc/lts.conf:%0a%3c %0a%3c ENCRYPT_SWAP=Y%0a%3c %0a%3c and install the cryptsetup package:%0a%3c %0a%3c chroot /opt/ltsp/i386 apt-get install cryptsetup%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c alternately, you can configure nbd-server the hard way:%0a%3c %0a%3c apt-get install nbd-server%0a%3c %0a%3c in /etc/nbd-server:%0a%3c %0a%3c NBD_PORT[0]=9210%0a%3c NBD_FILE[0]=/opt/ltsp/swap/swapfile.%25s%0a%3c NBD_SERVER_OPTS[0]=""%0a%3c %0a%3c invoke-rc.d nbd-server start%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c create a file for each possible ip address that will attempt%0a%3c to connect to the server:%0a%3c %0a%3c # size in megabytes%0a%3c size=100%0a%3c your_ip_addresses="10.0.2.2 10.0.2.3 10.0.2.4 ..."%0a%3c mkdir -p /opt/ltsp/swap/%0a%3c for a in $your_ip_addresse ; do%0a%3c   dd if=/dev/zero of=/opt/ltsp/swap/swapfile.$a bs=1024k count=$size%0a%3c done%0a%3c @]%0a\ No newline at end of file%0a
host:1239067635=189.35.184.218
